---
layout: layouts/product.njk
permalink: /integrators/hosted-pbx/
title: "Hosted PBX and VoiceTel Phone for integrators"
description: "Multi-tenant Hosted PBX and branded calling apps across web, desktop, and mobile — scale from one office to many customer locations."
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Integrators · Hosted PBX</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">Hosted PBX for one office or one hundred tenants.</h1>
			<p class="lede">VoiceTel Hosted PBX gives organizations a fully managed phone system tied directly to VoiceTel numbers, SIP routing, emergency-service configuration, and support. Built on VoiceML, designed for flexibility and carrier-grade resiliency.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact/">Become a partner {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--secondary btn--lg" href="/pbx/">Hosted PBX overview</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set diagram = {
				title: "A partner account holds many tenants; each tenant serves its own users and devices",
				nodes: [
					{ label: "Partner account", value: "One carrier relationship", meta: "many tenants", icon: "buildings" },
					{ label: "Tenant", value: "Portal scope · caller IDs", meta: "e911 records · users · CDRs", icon: "diagram-3", accent: true },
					{ label: "Users", value: "Extensions · devices", meta: "VoiceTel Phone", icon: "person-plus" }
				],
				links: [
					{ label: "per tenant", accent: true },
					{ label: "SIP", both: true }
				],
				meta: [
					{ k: "Tenancy", v: "multi-tenant from the ground up" },
					{ k: "Scale", v: "one office to many customer locations" },
					{ k: "Runtime", v: "VoiceML" }
				]
			} %}
			{% include "partials/v2/diagram.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="tenants" aria-labelledby="tenants-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">Multi-tenant</p>
				<h2 id="tenants-heading">Multi-tenant from the ground up, billed per tenant and per extension.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Each tenant in a partner account has its own portal scope, caller IDs, emergency-service records, users, and CDRs. Scale from one office to many customer locations.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pricing/#pbx-tenant">See PBX pricing</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set rates = [
					{ name: "PBX tenant", unit: "/ tenant / month", id: "pbx-tenant" },
					{ name: "PBX extension", unit: "/ extension / month", id: "pbx-extension" },
					{ name: "E911 record", unit: "/ record / month", id: "e911" },
					{ name: "Outbound minutes", unit: "US local · / min", id: "voice-out-us50", star: true },
					{ name: "Inbound minutes", unit: "US local · / min", id: "voice-in-local", star: true }
				] %}
				{%- set rateFootnote = "List rates. Volume tiers apply automatically in the <a href=\"/pricing/\">pricing calculator</a>." %}
				{% include "partials/v2/price-table.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="features" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">PBX features</p>
			<h2 id="features-heading">Hosted PBX features partners can package.</h2>
			<p class="lede">Extensions, voicemail, ring groups, business hours, attendant menus, and VoiceTel Phone users, managed per tenant.</p>
		</div>
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "person-vcard", title: "Extensions and users", body: "Manage users, extensions, caller ID, and device credentials." },
			{ icon: "envelope", title: "Voicemail", body: "Business voicemail workflows with notification and routing behavior." },
			{ icon: "diagram-3", title: "Ring groups", body: "Route calls to departments, teams, on-call groups, or shared business functions." },
			{ icon: "clock", title: "Business hours", body: "Schedules for open, closed, holiday, emergency, and after-hours routing." },
			{ icon: "list-check", title: "Attendant menus", body: "Simple IVR front doors for sales, support, billing, and general inquiries." },
			{ icon: "phone-vibrate", title: "VoiceTel Phone", body: "Pair hosted users with web, desktop, and mobile calling where enabled." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="phone" aria-labelledby="phone-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">VoiceTel Phone</p>
				<h2 id="phone-heading">Business calling across web, desktop, and mobile on one VoiceTel identity.</h2>
				<p class="lede">VoiceTel Phone gives users a consistent calling experience across browser, Windows, macOS, Linux, iOS, and Android, with provisioning tied to VoiceTel SIP credentials and account controls. A clean way to support remote workers, hybrid teams, deskless employees, mobile users, and customers who don't want to rely only on desk phones.</p>
				<div class="cta-row">
					<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/phone/">VoiceTel Phone overview</a>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set platforms = [
					{ icon: "code-slash", name: "Web", meta: "WebRTC · browser", href: "/phone/applications/web/" },
					{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "Windows", meta: "Desktop app", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/windows/" },
					{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "macOS", meta: "Desktop app", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/macos/" },
					{ icon: "hdd-stack", name: "Linux", meta: "Desktop app", href: "/phone/applications/desktop/linux/" },
					{ icon: "phone-vibrate", name: "iOS", meta: "Mobile app", href: "/phone/applications/mobile/ios/" },
					{ icon: "phone-vibrate", name: "Android", meta: "Mobile app", href: "/phone/applications/mobile/android/" }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/platform-grid.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>

		<h3 class="subsection-heading">Application features</h3>
		{%- set featureHeading = "h4" %}
		{%- set features = [
			{ icon: "telephone", title: "Web calling", body: "Place calls from the browser where WebRTC is supported." },
			{ icon: "layers", title: "Desktop apps", body: "Windows, macOS, and Linux users with the same VoiceTel identity." },
			{ icon: "phone-vibrate", title: "Mobile apps", body: "iOS and Android where mobile deployment is enabled." },
			{ icon: "shield-check", title: "WebRTC media", body: "Modern browser media with DTLS-SRTP where supported by the runtime." },
			{ icon: "record-circle", title: "Call recording", body: "Recording for training, quality assurance, or compliance workflows." },
			{ icon: "activity", title: "Diagnostics", body: "Call history, DTMF behavior, and SIP message logging for troubleshooting." },
			{ icon: "tag", title: "Private-label opportunities", body: "Custom branding and licensing for resellers and integrators." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/feature-grid.njk" %}

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Roll out PBX tenants under one carrier relationship.</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Per-tenant portal scope, caller IDs, e911 records, users, and CDRs.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/contact/">Contact partner sales {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/pbx/">Hosted PBX overview</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
